From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: winemac.drv: clip child client surfaces to their visible region

Modules: dlls/winemac.drv
Base: wine-11.16 + wine-staging v11.16 winemac.drv-no-flicker-patch (0000-*.patch)

A child window's GL/Vulkan/Metal client surface is a flat subview of the toplevel Cocoa
window, drawn above everything Win32 paints, and it ignored the child's visibility,
z-order and clipping. Switching between child views (Altium document tabs) left the old
Metal view on top, and child panels shown over a view were hidden under it.

Clip the view to the child's visible region (SYSRGN at monitor DPI; siblings above it are
always excluded, children per WS_CLIPCHILDREN) with a CAShapeLayer mask, and hide it when
nothing is visible. The clip is computed outside the win_data lock; the "is this the
presented view" check, mask and show/hide then happen together under it. The mask is set
before a view is shown and left alone while it is hidden, so no frame shows unclipped.
Windows that become toplevel drop the mask.

Known limitation: the clip is refreshed when win32u updates or presents the surface; a
child that stops presenting keeps its last clip until its own window changes.

